{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FORK RECORD (implementer, pre-review): the ticket AC asks that 'rebar explain <criterion-id>' document the pattern. With the operator placement ruling (no new criterion; language lands in the existing 'tests' and 'error-handling' code-review criteria), those criterion ids have NO per-criterion explain surface: rebar explain resolves plan-review criteria + the packaged guides only (src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py _explain; src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_guide.py). Default taken unless overridden: satisfy the documentation AC through the code-review author guide served by 'rebar explain review' (src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md), with two worked examples from the corpus (instances 1 and 6). Building a per-criterion explain surface for code-review ids would be new infrastructure contrary to the ruling's no-new-surface spirit; if that surface is wanted, it should be a follow-up ticket."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787353065981839001,"uuid":"5f7c6065-a5de-4e94-8648-449a47067de9"}